      "writtenOn": "2026-03-13T13:26:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What I don\u0027t like about this approach is we\u0027ll need to implement extra flags whenever we want something slightly different for deterministic.js. I would prefer just guaranteeing to the user that the scripts will be executed in the order they are passed to the CLI and then do:\n\n./cb.py --inject_scripts\u003ddeterministic.js,constant_random.js\n\nwhere constant_random.js overrides Math.random to be constant",
      "revId": "bbb1b3c7baf9e5c0016e53da4ecf95fc577392eb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "345e33c4_55d2d98e",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1246261
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-13T14:13:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see the benefits of your proposed approach, but there are downsides as well. I\u0027ll only list two; note that the first one is the major one.\n- Your approach does not store the value used during recording in the archive. That requires that this information be transmitted out of band and then reapplied during replay; failure to provide that value (or include constant_random.js) would lead to discrepancies between the recording and the replay. Those won\u0027t be easy to detect, but they\u0027ll have the potential for significant performance and power ramificaitons.\n- It is potentially confusing for a future developer to see overrides in one file and then wonder why they did not take effect; it would take some time to realise that these overrides where themselves overridden again later, possibly multiple times. It also requires that the developer carefully manage dependencies across these files, possibly in hard to maintain ways.",
      "parentUuid": "8d6dfd6b_e28202f7",
      "revId": "bbb1b3c7baf9e5c0016e53da4ecf95fc577392eb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cda923d7_19d981ad",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1339017
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-13T16:06:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Discussed offline. One point we raised is that, in terms of achieving consistent replay/recording behavior, one option would be to store deterministic.js completely into the archive at recording time. It comes with a trade-off, since in some cases we might want to change the behavior of those functions without recreating the archive.",
      "parentUuid": "345e33c4_55d2d98e",
      "revId": "bbb1b3c7baf9e5c0016e53da4ecf95fc577392eb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
