      "writtenOn": "2026-03-13T16:33:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In this context, `!\u003d\u003d` would be inferior, given that we have no reason to distinguish `undefined` and `null`; things would be less error-prone with them treated as equivalent (in this context).\n\nRun this code:\n```\nlet lhs, rhs;\n\nlhs \u003d null; rhs \u003d null;\nconsole.log(`(${lhs} \u003d\u003d ${rhs}) yields ${lhs \u003d\u003d rhs}.`);\nconsole.log(`(${lhs} \u003d\u003d\u003d ${rhs}) yields ${lhs \u003d\u003d\u003d rhs}.`);\n\nlhs \u003d 0; rhs \u003d null;\nconsole.log(`(${lhs} \u003d\u003d ${rhs}) yields ${lhs \u003d\u003d rhs}.`);\nconsole.log(`(${lhs} \u003d\u003d\u003d ${rhs}) yields ${lhs \u003d\u003d\u003d rhs}.`);\n\nlhs \u003d undefined; rhs \u003d null;\nconsole.log(`(${lhs} \u003d\u003d ${rhs}) yields ${lhs \u003d\u003d rhs}.`);\nconsole.log(`(${lhs} \u003d\u003d\u003d ${rhs}) yields ${lhs \u003d\u003d\u003d rhs}.`);\n```",
      "parentUuid": "67795415_f7b3c582",
